{"availability":"available","full":"hermes98761234/opamp-circuit-designer","name":"opamp-circuit-designer","description":"Op-amp circuit designer: amplifiers, Sallen-Key/MFB filters and Schmitt triggers with E-series parts, schematic and GBW-aware frequency response. Runs in the browser.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-10T06:32:37Z","updated":"2026-10-10T06:32:49Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hermes98761234.github.io/opamp-circuit-designer/","topics":["active-filter","calculator","electronics","github-pages","opamp","operational-amplifier","react","sallen-key","typescript","vite"],"demo":"https://hermes98761234.github.io/opamp-circuit-designer/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:09.055Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:09.055Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:09.055Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:09.055Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Pick an op-amp circuit, type the gain, cutoff or threshold you want, and get standard E-series resistor and capacitor values, a schematic, a results table and a frequency response that includes your op-amp's gain-bandwidth limit. Everything runs in your browser.","Try it: hermes98761234.github.io/opamp-circuit-designer"],"features":["Eleven circuits. Inverting, non-inverting, difference, instrumentation (three op-amps) and summing amplifiers, an integrator with a DC-gain limit, Sallen-Key low-pass and high-pass, multiple-feedback (Rauch) low-pass…","Real parts. Resistors from E6 to E192 and capacitors from E6 to E192. For gain-setting pairs and capacitor ratios it searches for the combination with the smallest error, not just the nearest value of each.","GBW-aware response. Magnitude and phase plots show the chosen op-amp (finite gain and gain-bandwidth) against an ideal one, with the -3 dB point marked. Presets for common op-amps (LM358, TL072,